    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy notice</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_title">Data processed</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_body">When Usage Access is granted, DigitsCore reads app names, package names, observed unlock events, and usage sessions and open counts for the top app while the screen is on and unlocked. Background playback with the screen off is not measured.</string>
    <string name="privacy_purpose_title">Purpose</string>
    <string name="privacy_purpose_body">This data is used only to calculate digital-use patterns and display scores and statistics in the app and notifications.</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage_title">Storage and transfer</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage_body">Results and settings are stored in an on-device SQLCipher-encrypted database protected by Android Keystore. Detailed sessions and five-minute scores last 30 days; hourly and daily usage, opens, scores and loss summaries last 365 days; minimal unlock and notification events last 48 hours. They are excluded from OS backup and device transfer. Nothing is sent to a server. Manual backups use password-based AES-256-GCM encryption.</string>
    <string name="privacy_choice_title">Your choices</string>
    <string name="privacy_choice_body">Detailed sessions and five-minute Core Index samples are retained for 30 days, minimal unlock and notification events for 25 hours, and daily usage and open-count aggregates for 365 days. An encrypted export includes details available at export time. You can hide lock-screen details, stop tracking, delete all history immediately, or revoke access in Android settings.</string>
